 ## Background
-Hierarchical sampling was introduced in the context of Neural Radiance Fields (NeRF) to improve the efficiency of volume rendering [S1, S2, unofficial]. The original NeRF paper by Mildenhall et al. used stratified sampling within intervals defined by a coarse network [S2, unofficial]. Later works, such as those by Drorke and others, refined this by explicitly using inverse CDF sampling on normalized weights to achieve importance sampling [S1, S3, unofficial]. This method has become a standard component in modern NeRF variants and volume rendering pipelines [S1, S5, unofficial].
+Hierarchical sampling was introduced in the context of Neural Radiance Fields (NeRF) to improve the efficiency of volume rendering [S1, S2, unofficial]. The original NeRF paper by Mildenhall et al. used stratified sampling within intervals defined by a coarse network [S2, unofficial]. Later works, such as those by Drorke and others, refined this by explicitly using inverse CDF sampling on normalized weights to achieve importance sampling [S1, S3, unofficial].
 
